WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.410
Near Caesarea Philippi, Jesus asks
his disciples a direct question:

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.590
who do you say that I am?

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.840
Peter answers: You are the Christ.

4
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.260
Jesus tells them to tell no one.

5
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.880
Then he speaks of himself in other words:

6
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.500
the Son of Man.

7
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:22.340
So what did Son of Man mean,
and why not simply say Messiah?

8
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:27.400
In this mission, you'll trace Son of God
and Son of Man back into the Old Testament,

9
00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.620
long before Jesus used them.

10
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.050
Then you'll sort his Son of Man sayings
into groups and test what scholars make

11
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.010
of them.

12
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.160
Your mission: find out
what Son of Man meant,

13
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.910
and why Jesus used it instead of Messiah.
